"] [:db/add "1efeba55-84f5-5363-86b8-c3a17d7c4c46" :answer-field/correct "bea06560-306b-5191-b859-68a659a93574"] [:db/ensure "1efeba55-84f5-5363-86b8-c3a17d7c4c46" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/id #uuid "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c"] [:db/add "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x{y}^{3}}{x+1}\n$$\n\nWork on a domain where all displayed expressions are defined."] [:db/add "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(\\frac{x}{x+1})\\cdot {y}^{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{x+1}\n$$"] [:db/add "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/answer-fields "1efeba55-84f5-5363-86b8-c3a17d7c4c46"] [:db/ensure "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186068842 :knowledge-point/questions "1f3824b9-c900-5e9e-8087-0cc8093edc0c"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "93dbdaeb-d6f4-556e-9c24-7230f1f4e393"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "generators/e2/e230c1fbfc7861f6eac7fd9fdf71fa88c2529935343587027c5a4aea3b94088c/17592186068842.py"] [:db/add 17592186068842 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] [:db/ensure 17592186068842 :knowledge-point/validate]]
